    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d41-a1">

                <pb facs="0135" n="1095" sameAs="frus:frus1888p2/pg1095"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 220.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Heimké to Mr.
                            Porter.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Consulate</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Chihuahua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1887-10-29"><hi rendition="#italic">October</hi> 29,
                        1887</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 15.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to report that after an
                    incarceration in the <hi rendition="#italic">cárcel pública</hi> here for a
                    period of close upon three years of Mr. Henry Brudigam, an American citizen, for
                    the alleged murder of one Domingo Steiner, a former jeweler of Chihuahua, he has
                    been released from his imprisonment, the courts having found him “not guilty.”
                    Mr. Brudigam informs me that he will leave in a few days for the United States,
                    where he intends to employ counsel for the prosecution of an indemnity claim for
                    his long and unjust imprisonment here.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wm. Heimké.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
